From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Steinhauf <daniel@steinhauf.eu>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:18:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: realtek: rtl8365mb: provide field_get() on v6.18

The backported VLAN code reads the per-port accept-frame type with
field_get(), whose mask is not a compile-time constant. Mainline added
the lowercase field_get() to <linux/bitfield.h> after v6.18, so the
backport does not build on v6.18 without it.

Define it locally, guarded by #ifndef, until the kernel provides it.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Steinhauf <daniel@steinhauf.eu>
---
 drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_vlan.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_vlan.c b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_vlan.c
index 64dd8d90a..1f2b40dc7 100644
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_vlan.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_vlan.c
@@ -52,6 +52,15 @@
 #include <linux/lockdep.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 
+/*
+ * v6.18 has FIELD_GET() only, which needs a constant mask. The per-port
+ * accept-frame mask below is not constant. Mainline gained field_get() in
+ * <linux/bitfield.h> after v6.18; drop this once the kernel has it.
+ */
+#ifndef field_get
+#define field_get(_mask, _reg)	(((_reg) & (_mask)) >> (ffs(_mask) - 1))
+#endif
+
 /* CVLAN (i.e. VLAN4k) table entry layout, u16[3] */
 #define RTL8365MB_CVLAN_ENTRY_SIZE			3 /* 48-bits */
 #define RTL8365MB_CVLAN_ENTRY_D0_MBR_MASK		GENMASK(7, 0)
